ity March as a significant event\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Unity March is a significant event taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza. This event is a key factor in the community's dynamics and could be a potential source of threat, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. The relationship between the march and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Relationships (39)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Role of Tribune Spotlight\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity March taking place in Verdant Oasis Plaza. This suggests that the event has attracted media attention, which could amplify its impact on the community. The role of Tribune Spotlight could be significant in shaping public perception of the event and the entities involved. [Data: Relationships (40)]\"\n        }}\n    ]\n}}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n2008,ZINC,\"Zinc is an essential trace element and micronutrient that plays a critical role in various bodily functions, including immune response, protein synthesis, wound healing, and cognitive development. It is particularly important for the growth and development of children and is often included in infant formulas to support immune function and overall health. The recommended daily intake of zinc varies by age and gender, with general guidelines suggesting a daily intake of 10-20 mg for adults and specific recommendations for pediatric patients.\n\nZinc deficiency is frequently observed in various health conditions, including chronic liver disease, cirrhosis, inflammatory bowel disease, and after biliopancreatic diversion surgeries. It is also common in patients with eating disorders, cystic fibrosis, and those undergoing parenteral nutrition. Deficiencies can lead to significant health issues, such as impaired wound healing, immune dysfunction, and alterations in taste perception. In critically ill patients, zinc supplementation is recommended to support recovery, and it is also suggested for children experiencing acute diarrhea, as per WHO and UNICEF guidelines.\n\nZinc is involved in numerous biological processes, including DNA replication and transcription, and it helps reduce infections, particularly in older adults. While zinc is crucial for health, excessive levels can contribute to oxidative stress and neurodegeneration. Therefore, monitoring zinc levels is important, especially in patients with specific health conditions or those at risk of deficiency. Zinc supplements are available in various forms, including capsules and tablets, to help individuals meet their nutritional needs.\",52\r\n2014,SELENIO,\"SELENIO, or selenium, is an essential trace mineral and micronutrient that plays a critical role in various bodily functions, particularly in antioxidant defense and thyroid function. It is recommended as a supplement for patients, with a suggested daily intake of 100 mg, although specific dosage recommendations may vary based on factors such as age and gender. Selenium is known for its antioxidant properties, which help protect against free radicals, and it is a cofactor for the enzyme glutathione peroxidase, crucial for maintaining cellular health.\n\nDeficiency in selenium has been associated with several health issues, including coronary pathology, immunosuppression, and certain neoplasias. In particular, its deficiency can lead to reversible myocardiopathy and irreversible encephalitis in patients with inflammatory bowel disease. Additionally, selenium deficiency is linked to the development of goiter due to its role in thyroid hormone synthesis. While selenium is generally rare in deficiency, it can be particularly low in patients with chronic liver disease, those undergoing prolonged dialysis, and individuals who have had certain surgeries.\n\nSelenium supplementation is advised with caution, especially in patients with renal insufficiency, and its use in oncology is not sufficiently supported by evidence. It has been suggested as a protective factor against cardiovascular diseases and cancer due to its anti-inflammatory and antioxidant properties. Regular monitoring of selenium levels in the blood is recommended for individuals on restricted diets or those not supplementing regularly. Overall, selenium is a vital micronutrient that contributes significantly to metabolic processes and immune health.\",20\r\n2009,COBRE,\"Cobre, or copper, is a trace mineral that plays a crucial role in various physiological processes, including iron metabolism, the formation of red blood cells, and the development of connective tissue. It is an essential micronutrient that is particularly important for pediatric patients, with specific dosage recommendations ranging from 0.5 to 1.5 mg according to daily guidelines. Copper deficiency is common, especially after procedures like biliopancreatic diversion, and it often presents asymptomatically. Additionally, copper levels are routinely tested to assess nutritional status and identify potential deficiencies in individuals, particularly those with eating disorders. In summary, cobre is vital for growth, bone mineralization, and the production of red blood cells, highlighting its importance in maintaining overall health.\",7\r\n2413,PACIENTE ANCIANO,\"El paciente anciano es un individuo que puede presentar alteraciones en la masticación y deglución, lo que requiere modificaciones en su dieta y atención especial.\",14\r\n8770,MICRONUTRIENT DEFICIENCY,\"Common in patients undergoing bariatric surgery, it can be prevented or treated early with proper follow-up and supplementation.\",11\r\n2017,NUTRICIONES COMERCIALIZADAS,\"Commercial nutrition formulations are ready-to-use mixtures produced by the pharmaceutical industry, containing macronutrients but lacking